# NOTICE

`opencode-unlimited-proxy` is a thin orchestration bundle. It contains **no
vendored copy of the inference engine**: the engine runs from a public
container image. What lives in this repository is Docker Compose glue plus
build context for two helper images.

## Third-party components

### Cloudflare WARP rotator — `stack/warp/`
Files: `rotator.py`, `manager.py`, `LICENSE` — **copied verbatim** from
[`alztrk/opencode-ip-rotator`](https://github.com/alztrk/opencode-ip-rotator)
(`Dockerfile.warp`). Licensed under the MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 alztrk.
The original license text is preserved in `stack/warp/LICENSE`.

`rotator.py` registers a Cloudflare WARP tunnel inside the container, runs it in
its own network namespace, and re-establishes the tunnel on the
`WARP_ROTATION_INTERVAL` cycle so the container's egress address changes.

Files: `Dockerfile`, `entrypoint.sh` — **derived from** the same project's
`Dockerfile.warp`, with one substantive change: upstream's entrypoint accepted the
Cloudflare terms of service automatically (`warp-cli --accept-tos ...`). Here
that acceptance is an explicit opt-in via `WARP_ACCEPT_TOS=1`, so no legal
agreement is entered on a user's behalf. The remainder of the build is unchanged.

### CONNECT proxy — `stack/tinyproxy/`
Files: `Dockerfile`, `tinyproxy.conf`

Thin `tinyproxy` packaging on top of Alpine Linux (`apk add tinyproxy`).
tinyproxy is licensed **GPL-2.0**; it is installed as an Alpine package at
build time, not vendored here, so no source-distribution obligation arises.

### Inference engine — pulled at runtime, not distributed here
`ghcr.io/jasonxu114514/opencode2api:latest` — [`jasonxu114514/opencode2api`](https://github.com/jasonxu114514/opencode2api),
**GPL-3.0**. This repository ships only a Compose reference to that image.
If you redistribute a derivative that includes the engine, GPL-3.0 applies to
that derivative.

### OpenCode upstream
Requests are forwarded to `https://opencode.ai/inference`. opencode.ai is a
third-party service operated independently of this project; no affiliation or
endorsement is claimed.

## Scope of the license
The MIT license in `LICENSE` covers this repository's own files: the Compose
files, `stack/config.json`, `stack/generate-compose.py`, `stack/tinyproxy/`,
`stack/warp/entrypoint.sh`, `scripts/`, `docs/`, and `README.md`. It does not
relicense the components above; `stack/warp/rotator.py` and
`stack/warp/manager.py` remain under alztrk's MIT license.

## Terms of service, not licences
Two separate questions are easy to conflate. Publishing this repository raises
no licensing issue. *Running* it involves services with their own terms — see
the "Legal and terms of service" section of `README.md`, which quotes the
relevant Cloudflare Application Terms of Service and explains why the Cloudflare
terms are accepted only through an explicit `WARP_ACCEPT_TOS=1` opt-in.
